<title>USA: Newark, N.J., to vote in March on stadium -- paper.</title>
<headline>Newark, N.J., to vote in March on stadium -- paper.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-01-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Newark, N.J.'s city council Tuesday scheduled March 11 for a public referendum on whether to extend an $11 million city guarantee to a $22 million stadium project, the Star Ledger reported Wednesday.</p>
<p>Council members said the vote may be meaningless, however, since the Essex County Improvement Authority plans to sell the bonds for the project without a city guarantee.</p>
<p>But council members said they did not wish to ignore a referendum sought by 3,200 voters who signed a petition asking for the referendum, the paper said.</p>
<p>The project, known as the Ironbound sportsplex, features a 6,000-seat baseball stadium and an adjacent 6,000-seat soccer stadium.</p>
<p>--Steven Dickson, 212-859-1652</p>
